Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:02.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is an existential issue for us.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.60,0:00:05.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,We could easily stop, but if we stop today, we lose.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.17,0:00:10.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Functionality, capability, safety, security, they're all at exactly the same place.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.11,0:00:20.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Priority number one.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.00,0:00:22.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,This this is America's superpowers.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.80,0:00:23.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.20,0:00:31.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um in a lot of ways the intellectual property creation capability of our nation is unlike anything else in the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.85,0:00:33.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for that is we attract the world's best.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.96,0:00:34.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.40,0:00:39.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, we are the place where they want to come and build their lives because of the opportunity it provides,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.80,0:00:48.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,the freedom that that she offers, the opportunity that it provides, the spirit of of invention and entrepreneurialism and of the can-do attitude.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.93,0:00:52.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, in the United States everything is is possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.52,0:00:53.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.20,0:00:55.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,We start with of course it's possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.08,0:00:56.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,Of course we could do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.77,0:01:01.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Instead of instead of you know, I I do a lot of travel and of course you can't do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.56,0:01:04.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,Of course you know, In other places. in other in other places.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.33,0:01:05.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we take it for granted.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.00,0:01:06.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,It does.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.40,0:01:15.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,But the spirit, the the the energy um that comes around with the culture that we've created here, Yeah. um it's just can't be understated.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.90,0:01:26.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And And so I think the flow, the inflow of intellectual property into this into this country is unlike anything else the world's ever seen.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.28,0:01:26.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.76,0:01:27.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we want that.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.68,0:01:34.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,We want all of the world's great minds to come here, bring their great ideas, you know, make them realize them here, Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.16,0:01:39.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,realize them here and let us, you know, let us let us keep that flywheel going.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.33,0:01:42.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, I really it's a it's a delicate system.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.32,0:01:43.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a delicate balance.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.53,0:01:45.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,I get it's a delicate balance.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.19,0:01:47.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,I get and so we have to do it lawfully.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.10,0:01:48.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have to do it rightfully.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.92,0:01:50.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but we we surely want to do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.64,0:01:51.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, for sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.48,0:01:54.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I want to start high level just kind of where we are.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.31,0:02:00.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then I want to dig down a little bit into the safety and regulation and getting this right.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.11,0:02:02.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,Where we are in terms of the compute build out.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.53,0:02:08.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then finally we're going to finish up you know, drilling in a little bit to Nvidia's growth and and and and what's going on there.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.84,0:02:11.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,But you've been really good at calling the future, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.69,0:02:17.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Two years ago we were sitting here and you said that the market was dramatically underestimating the amount of compute
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.80,0:02:22.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,build out that was going to be required and was going to happen over the course of the next 5 years.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.55,0:02:28.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,You You said it's not going to be a trillion, it's going to be 2 trillion at a minimum in terms of cumulative compute build out.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.21,0:02:29.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And of course now we're over that.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.96,0:02:33.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,You said before everybody was thinking about it that inference, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.35,0:02:38.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Compute was going to 1 billion X because of inference time reasoning and thinking.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.28,0:02:45.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and then last year of course, before we saw Opus 4.6, before we saw Claude code, you said we're entering the age of agents, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.91,0:02:49.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Where we're going to unlock a lot of these capabilities.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.21,0:02:52.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and of course we saw Opus 4.6 and Claude code really took off.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.02,0:02:54.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,So where are we now, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.72,0:02:58.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,We We Elon and Sam and And only three things that I said that came true.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.58,0:02:59.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's another 200.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.63,0:03:01.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Why don't you just keep on going?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.44,0:03:04.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,That I just let that be the podcast.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.28,0:03:11.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I just So So So our investor day in a couple weeks is on, you know, entering the singularity, this acceleration.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.36,0:03:17.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have Elon and Sam and Demis all say, "Hey, we're in the foothills or entering the singularity."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.96,0:03:21.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have, you know, model solving Navier-Stokes, as you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.04,0:03:26.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so when you look into your crystal ball, where are we?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.18,0:03:27.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,And are we inflecting?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.73,0:03:34.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Are we accelerating, you know, into a different phase of superintelligence?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.04,0:03:38.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um And so let let's unpack that.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.73,0:03:41.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,First First of all,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.24,0:03:48.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's very fairly logical why the amount of compute that we're going to need is a billion times more than where we were just recently,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.52,0:03:49.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,let's say call it last year.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.82,0:03:57.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for that is because thinking and problem solving takes a lot more,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.20,0:04:04.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, inferences than repeating something, regurgitating something that you memorized.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.53,0:04:12.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,So when you're a ChatGPT, you give it a prompt, most of that most of that knowledge was encoded into the large language model.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.76,0:04:15.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Unfortunately, of course, it hallucinated.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.90,0:04:24.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so the next click was it was it was a generative, but it was also grounded or conditioned by ground truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.28,0:04:25.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.76,0:04:29.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,It would have to go out and do a search, do a quick search, comes back with the ground truth,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.34,0:04:34.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,and then from that conditioning augment it with his own own what it already learned,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.92,0:04:39.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,pre-training, and it would generate new new whatever the answer is.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.71,0:04:46.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, most of most of the things that we want to really do that are that are interesting requires you to to to reason step by step,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.57,0:04:49.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,to come up with several options, plan,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.21,0:04:50.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,and you might decide,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.50,0:04:58.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,"Let's see how these things all roll out and then based on based on the answers of all of those I reflect on the best answers so far,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.52,0:04:59.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,the best path so far.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.81,0:05:03.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,I might choose one or two or three of them, roll them out.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.28,0:05:03.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.60,0:05:05.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, prune the rest of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.11,0:05:06.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then just keep on doing this.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.47,0:05:14.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you know, people we do this that's the reason why why we say um, great strategists love strategic optionality.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.20,0:05:19.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,You don't want to prune things too fast on the one hand, but you you also have to optimize your resources.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.92,0:05:21.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, AI's are doing that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.80,0:05:26.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, so so they're they're keeping their strategic optionality, they're rolling things out,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.60,0:05:31.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,they're pruning, um, they're they're reflecting, they're pruning, so on and so forth.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.15,0:05:36.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,And all of that thinking all of that exploration just takes a lot more compute.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.15,0:05:42.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and not on top of that, because it's able to now do productive things, we're going to use it for more things.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.67,0:05:46.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so the compounding of both it uses more compute to do its job,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.49,0:05:50.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,but it's doing a good job and therefore we're going to we're going to hire it to do more jobs.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.32,0:05:50.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.00,0:05:51.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.36,0:05:52.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so that all compounds.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.98,0:05:53.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.22,0:05:59.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,at this point I would I would say that the big observation from last year is that that on the
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.72,0:06:03.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,one hand we want the models to get better and better and we we still want the models to get better.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.29,0:06:06.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the scaling laws of models are are going to continue.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.82,0:06:14.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,However, the attachment of a harness, basically the exoskeleton of the large language model.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.32,0:06:14.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.80,0:06:22.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, kind of the body of the brain that allows it to um, manage manage working memory, manage knowledge.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.51,0:06:29.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do you go from working memory to short term, to long term, to basically formulating your knowledge graph, which is what we all do.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.03,0:06:36.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,We kind of think about, "Hey, you know, what did I learn and how does it fit into everything that I know in the past?"
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.30,0:06:39.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you know how when we we go to bed, we do compaction.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.45,0:06:44.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Things that don't make sense, we kind of or don't matter, we kind of eventually forget.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.48,0:06:47.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,But the things that kind of matter somehow it gets reconnected.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.17,0:06:49.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we're doing that kind of offline.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.34,0:06:55.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we got working memory, we have offline knowledge extraction and creation, knowledge graph creation.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.04,0:06:58.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um that whole part of memory is a big deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.56,0:07:00.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,The other thing is, of course, tool use.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.92,0:07:01.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.16,0:07:08.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we we've taught these tools, these uh AIs, how to interact with uh the most important tools that the hum- humans ever made.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.29,0:07:13.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, it's no different than uh if you were if you were a robot comes into our house,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.62,0:07:18.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh it's more likely you're going to use all the tools that I have in the house than to go off and build it from scratch.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.85,0:07:25.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so uh so SPICE is still going to be useful and um Verilog will be useful and uh simulators will be useful and you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.77,0:07:33.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,design compilers and and and you know, Photoshop and AutoCAD and you know, the CATIA and all the Siemens tools.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.72,0:07:37.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,All of these different tools that we've been using to run our company, build our company,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.34,0:07:41.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,design things, operate things, they're all going to be great tools for the agents to use.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.37,0:07:44.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,But the agents had to learn how to use it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.19,0:07:54.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so these two areas knowledge, knowledge um and working memory and um tool use, huge unlocks in the last year.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.32,0:07:54.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.60,0:07:59.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,So now all of the sudden you could you could put these large language models
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.46,0:08:06.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,encapsulated in their um harness or exoskeleton and you can put them into your company,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.80,0:08:11.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,connect them to uh the the information, the ground truth that you have,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.40,0:08:15.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,connect them to the the tools that they can use, and all of a sudden they start doing amazing things.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.89,0:08:19.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now the the easiest part uh frankly was coding.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.72,0:08:20.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.12,0:08:23.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's kind of the the the first on-ramp, you know, to useful work.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.94,0:08:25.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and in a lot of ways,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.48,0:08:30.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh coding is easy because both the customer and the work the the
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.70,0:08:37.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,tools that they use are fairly accustomed to uh things that has tremendous use,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.70,0:08:40.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,but are not extremely easy to use.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.26,0:08:46.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so in the early days of coding, it's it wasn't extremely easy to deploy, um but software engineers found a way.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.94,0:08:54.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, so now now I think the next click for us is now uh and and you guys have probably been playing with Astra, OpenAI's Astra.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.77,0:08:58.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's really fantastic, and we're using it in all these different places.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.15,0:09:06.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, now the next the next phase of these these agents, they're able to do, you know, design work and a lot of creative marketing work,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.88,0:09:13.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,and we're using it to go you take a picture and give it to Astra, it literally recreates it into CAD.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.84,0:09:14.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.32,0:09:14.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.80,0:09:16.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,It recreates it in the into the the CAD.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.96,0:09:20.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, which is incredible, because we need the CAD Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.28,0:09:24.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,so that we can we can interact with the CAD and make fine-tuning and adjust.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.76,0:09:28.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, Astra could really give us the the first initial implementation.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.54,0:09:30.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Incredibly productive.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.12,0:09:38.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you take you take Astra and and but you know, the the latest release and you apply to all of these different different domains.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.24,0:09:45.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I I think that that besides software engineering, you know, we're going to see designers and builders and creators and you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.19,0:09:49.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,this whole area, scientists, and you know, all of all of this whole unlocking.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.60,0:09:57.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, the challenge, of course, is how do we deploy agents safely and securely into the world's enterprise?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.39,0:10:01.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is exactly the same question again with safety and security.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.08,0:10:04.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and and and and we'll talk about it. about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.30,0:10:05.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,We'll we'll we'll come in on that.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.43,0:10:11.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,What what I'm what I'm struck by is that all of this occurred this year with OpenAI and Anthropic having,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.80,0:10:15.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,I don't know, two, three gigawatts of compute each, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.12,0:10:20.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, relatively small amount of compute relative to what's coming, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.20,0:10:21.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, again,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.40,0:10:31.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,what I'm interested in is the way the economy generally works or people model the economy or they model a company is linear deceleration.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.82,0:10:35.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're not very good at modeling acceleration.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.64,0:10:37.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,But here we have this double exponential.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.57,0:10:41.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have massive amount of new compute coming on board.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.20,0:10:47.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if OpenAI and Anthropic are, I don't know, three to five x'ing their compute next year, does it stand to reason?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.78,0:10:50.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, we solved Navier-Stokes.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.16,0:10:54.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,We'll look back at this and say that was a tiny amount of compute and intelligence,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.66,0:10:59.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,the worst intelligence we're ever going to have from here forward, solving a a millennium problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.04,0:11:06.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,So when you look at what's coming online next year, you know, do you expect that we're going to have major breakthroughs in,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.48,0:11:13.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, long-running agentic uh uh problems that that that we can use these swarms of agents on?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.80,0:11:16.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, Navier-Stokes is is really a great example.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.30,0:11:22.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um remember, uh OpenAI did not solve Navier-Stokes from nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.12,0:11:22.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.76,0:11:29.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,They solved it from the foundation of a lot of great scientists, a lot of great mathematicians, and a lot of great previous work.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.36,0:11:35.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Earlier I said, we're at we're at kind of the tipping point of a lot of these different fields.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.24,0:11:35.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.64,0:11:43.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because we're kind of at that phase, that that point with Navier-Stokes, with a great deal of foundational work already been done.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.39,0:11:49.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,If we could just apply the exhaustive exploration of AI Yes.
