Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.32,0:12:42.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um In the In the coming years, you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.58,0:12:50.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,my expectation is is that the the cost of intelligence would fall fairly fairly quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.36,0:12:51.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.24,0:12:55.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for that is because obviously we're bringing more compute online.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.20,0:12:57.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um these models are getting smarter.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.80,0:12:59.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,When you're smarter, you could be more efficient.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.80,0:13:00.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.48,0:13:06.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so the combination of these two things, the the cost of intelligence will come down, which is which is of course what they want.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.72,0:13:07.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.00,0:13:08.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is no different than Moore's law.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.59,0:13:17.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you go back 30 somewhat years, we we have three decades of computing cost decreasing by a factor of two every single year.
