Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.36,0:13:24.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and we want intelligence cost to decrease by a factor of two or 20 every single
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.41,0:13:29.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,year because we the consumption of it is going to It's going to more than up for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.32,0:13:29.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's Jevons paradox.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.92,0:13:30.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.40,0:13:31.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,More than make up for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.44,0:13:38.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,And And so there's there's a massive empty space in the world that wants to be filled, empty vacuum of of of opportunity.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.02,0:13:41.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And And we just got to get get the cost down.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.48,0:13:47.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I I guess what stands out to me about Navier-Stokes is that they had 10,000 agents working together.
